    "result_text": "The AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and all 2 tests pass with a clean `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `locality` derivation from an owner's city using the fixed table (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD, else `UNKNOWN`).\n\nChanges, each placed to keep responsibilities small and reusable:\n\n1. **`model/CityRegion.java`** (new) \u2014 a small single-responsibility class owning the fixed city-to-region lookup table and one `regionFor(city)` method returning the canonical region or `\"UNKNOWN\"`. Giving the table its own home keeps `Owner` from becoming a catch-all and lets future region-based rules (postcode/timezone, hinted at in the tests) reuse it.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a pure derived getter `getLocality()` that delegates to `CityRegion.regionFor(city)`, matching the existing derived-getter pattern (`getInitials`, `getMembershipTier`, `getMembershipNumber`).\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared `locality` as a `readOnly` string on the `Owner` schema, alongside the other derived fields. MapStruct maps it automatically by matching getter name, so the value surfaces at `$.locality` in the JSON response with no mapper change needed.\n\nBoth the known-city (`Sydney \u2192 NSW`) and unknown-city (`\u2192 UNKNOWN`) acceptance tests pass.",
